{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 5-10 EUR when the market is in a downtrend (prices falling from ~70 to ~55), failing to capture the magnitude of the decline.",
    "Apply aggressive mean reversion after sentiment spikes: When sentiment history shows a negative shock (-1.00) followed by a price spike (e.g., 65.80), the model incorrectly assumes a slow, linear recovery. Instead, apply a sharp correction to anticipate a rapid drop back to the lower mean (~53-55).",
    "Reduce forecast horizon lag: The model exhibits a 'flat-line' behavior, predicting near-constant values or very slow growth. Adjust forecasts to reflect the actual volatility and faster oscillation of the true price path, particularly in the 10-20 day horizon.",
    "Ignore positive sentiment drift in bear markets: Positive sentiment values (0.20) in the history do not correlate with sustained price increases in this dataset. Do not allow positive sentiment to bias the forecast upward when the underlying trend is bearish."
  ]
}
